<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Treaty of San Ildefonso</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1777">1777</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Treaty of San Ildefonso (1777) · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-portuguese-war-1776-1777">Spanish–Portuguese War (1776–1777)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Treaty of San Ildefonso was signed on 1 October 1777 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and Portugal at the royal palace of La Granja de San Ildefonso, ending their war over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a>. Portugal gave up Colonia del Sacramento and the Banda Oriental to Spain, which returned the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-catarina">Santa Catarina</a>. The treaty also defined much of the border between their South American empires.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-treaty-of-san-ildefonso.jpg" alt="First Treaty of San Ildefonso" width="320" height="362" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nagihuin · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Imperios_Espa%C3%B1ol_y_Portugu%C3%A9s_1790.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
